<div class="key-takeaways"><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul>
<li>You do not need a public adjuster for every claim. Small, straightforward claims with a responsive insurer are often fine to handle yourself.</li>
<li>Professional help tends to make the most sense on large, complex, delayed, underpaid, or denied claims, or when you lack the time to manage the process.</li>
<li>A public adjuster is licensed by the Texas Department of Insurance and represents only the policyholder; the insurer’s adjuster represents the insurer.</li>
